# Testing — 3 Níveis

## 1. Unit Tests (Domain)

Testam domain entities e value objects. **Sem mocks, sem banco, sem framework.**

```typescript
// test/unit/client.entity.spec.ts
describe('Client Entity', () => {
  it('should transition from pending_documents to document_validation', () => {
    const client = ClientFactory.create({ status: 'pending_documents' });
    const checklist = ChecklistFactory.allUploaded();
    client.submitForAnalysis(checklist);
    expect(client.status).toBe('document_validation');
  });

  it('should throw when submitting with missing documents', () => {
    const client = ClientFactory.create({ status: 'pending_documents' });
    const checklist = ChecklistFactory.withMissing(['balance_sheet_dre']);
    expect(() => client.submitForAnalysis(checklist))
      .toThrow(MissingDocumentsException);
  });
});
```

**Cobertura alvo:** 90%+ nas domain entities.

## 2. Integration Tests (Use Cases)

Testam use-cases com repositories reais (banco de teste) ou in-memory.

```typescript
// test/integration/submit-client.use-case.spec.ts
describe('SubmitClientUseCase', () => {
  it('should submit client and emit event', async () => {
    const useCase = new SubmitClientUseCase(inMemoryClientRepo, inMemoryChecklistService);
    await useCase.execute({ clientId: 'abc-123' });
    expect(inMemoryClientRepo.findById('abc-123')).resolves.toHaveProperty('status', 'document_validation');
  });
});
```

## 3. E2E Tests (Endpoints)

Testam o endpoint HTTP completo (auth → guard → controller → use-case → DB).

- Usam `supertest` com app NestJS bootstrapped.
- Banco de teste isolado (reset entre suites).
- Testam happy path + error paths + permissões (RBAC).

## Convenções

- Arquivo de teste ao lado do arquivo testado ou em `test/{unit|integration|e2e}/`.
- Sufixo `.spec.ts` para unit e integration, `.e2e-spec.ts` para e2e.
- Factories em `test/factories/` para criar entities de teste.
- Sem `console.log` em testes. Assertions explícitas.
- Todo bug fix acompanha um teste que reproduz o bug.
